body:
So, after a bit of digging, I may have found where it goes wrong.

When Godot receives a request over network, it processes it in `DebugAdapterProtocol::process_message`:

https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/53be3b78d1634406f1fb29e3802c608a5f5104a1/editor/debugger/debug_adapter/debug_adapter_protocol.cpp#L848-L851

It parses JSON and puts the data into `params` dictionary. This JSON contains `seq` key which gets deserialized as a float (even though the number appears to be an integer, is this expected behavior?). When Godot prepares the response, it assigns this key's value to response's `request_seq` key:

https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/53be3b78d1634406f1fb29e3802c608a5f5104a1/editor/debugger/debug_adapter/debug_adapter_parser.cpp#L73

Now `request_seq` is also a float. Godot serializes response into JSON and sends it back to the editor, and since https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/47502 always serializes floats with trailing `.0`,  `request_seq` is sent as `1.0`.

One workaround would be to cast to int before assigning to `request_seq`:

```diff
--- a/editor/debugger/debug_adapter/debug_adapter_parser.cpp
+++ b/editor/debugger/debug_adapter/debug_adapter_parser.cpp
@@ -70,7 +70,7 @@ Dictionary DebugAdapterParser::prepare_base_event() const {
 Dictionary DebugAdapterParser::prepare_success_response(const Dictionary &p_params) const {
        Dictionary response;
        response["type"] = "response";
-       response["request_seq"] = p_params["seq"];
+       response["request_seq"] = (int)p_params["seq"];
        response["command"] = p_params["command"];
        response["success"] = true;

@@ -80,7 +80,7 @@ Dictionary DebugAdapterParser::prepare_success_response(const Dictionary &p_para
 Dictionary DebugAdapterParser::prepare_error_response(const Dictionary &p_params, DAP::ErrorType err_type, const Dictionary &variables) const {
        Dictionary response, body;
        response["type"] = "response";
-       response["request_seq"] = p_params["seq"];
+       response["request_seq"] = (int)p_params["seq"];
        response["command"] = p_params["command"];
        response["success"] = false;
        response["body"] = body;

```

With this change everything works as expected. Is this something that should be fixed on server side (Godot) or client side (Zed editor)?
